WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Brazil is heading to a presidential runoff

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.200
after the top two finishers in Sunday's election

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.360
were unable to secure enough votes for an outright victory.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.920
In combat, Luis Enazio Lula de Silva

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.520
will face Senator Flavio Bolsonaro,

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.040
the son of former President Jair Bolsonaro,

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.720
who is currently serving a 27-year sentence

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.960
for plotting a coup after losing the 2022 election.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.730
The runoff is set for the 25th of October.

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.730
Brazil's presidential election

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:33.950
is heading into a second round, left his president Lula de Silva is fighting to extend

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:39.990
his time in office for the fourth non-consecutive term.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:47.150
We have the second round, and the runoff is the moment of truth. It's time to show the

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:55.210
true picture of Brazil, because today is the Brazil we want. So starting tomorrow, we're

00:00:55.210 --> 00:01:00.030
launching a new campaign.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:05.770
Lula's rival Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president Shire Bolsonaro, is promising

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.450
a return to the right-wing policies of his family.

